 "confidence": "medium",
 "notes": "Single 22-way edge connector, rear view; the drawing names none, so it is called P1. Letters and numbers are opposite contacts, each labelled separately. Title block names only M461 (Input Module, 461-04-002, ISS. 2, DRN. DM, DATE SEPT 76); the file is filed under M461M. Pairs with the same label on both sides (MIC IN A/1, LINE IN L/10, FB/RS outputs, LEFT/RIGHT OUT, etc.) read as balanced pairs but no +/- is drawn, so ports use 'a' (letter) / 'b' (number). MIC SHIELD is on 2 only; B, C/3 and K/9 are blank. FB 2, FB 1, RS 2, RS 1 (D/4 - H/7) are bracketed 'OUT' on both sides. SOLO/CUE (J/8) has no direction drawn; recorded as bus. Inserts are my interpretation: BOOSTER AMP / CH ON and PHASE SWITCH / OUTPUT AMP are adjacent rows drawn strapped together by brackets on both sides, i.e. a break in the channel path brought to the connector and normalled by the strap; send/return direction follows the signal path order (booster amp out to channel-on, phase switch out to output amp in). Control lines (LINE/MIC MUTE, SOLO, CH ON CONTROL) recorded as control_in, CH ON LAMP as control_out; directions are not drawn. +24 VOLT on Y (separate from +25 VOLT on 21) recorded as power."
}